# MIB text is compared byte for byte against what its publisher serves
# (see mib-sources.json). Git's end-of-line filters would rewrite that
# text on checkout, so a Windows working copy would report every tracked
# module as diverging and a patch cut on one would not apply on the
# other. Treat everything under src/ as opaque bytes.
src/** -text

# The patches are cut against those bytes and must survive the same way.
scripts/mib-patches/** -text
